#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Time-resolved directional analysis of the Sharif pentagon air-shower array.

This single-file program reconstructs all 44 DAQ runs, applies the calibrated
five-detector plane-front selection, forms Nside=16 Galactic maps, estimates
the background with within-run four-hour time reassignment, and calibrates the
look-elsewhere effect with an independent randomized ensemble. The primary
search is restricted to the 20% of statistically valid directions with the
largest expected 8-degree-aperture occupancy, and observed excess Z ranks
directions only within that fixed high-occupancy domain. Ten spatially
distinct directions are retained from the full archive and each of six
equal-live-exposure intervals for counterpart follow-up. The program also
performs the LHAASO/FAVA audits and exact source-centered 8-degree targeted
source tests used in the manuscript. HEALPix-cell statistics are retained only
for the calibrated map search and are kept explicitly distinct from exact
source-centered aperture statistics. The program generates the analysis
figures and result tables and prints a
complete numerical cross-check block to the console.

Required packages: numpy, pandas, scipy, matplotlib. Astropy is optional. No manual catalog directory is required: authoritative
catalog tables are acquired automatically at the start of a run and cached with
SHA-256 fingerprints in the V12 output directory. VizieR catalogs use the
official ASU-TSV interface with mirror fallback; HEASARC catalogs use VO cone
search with legacy-cone and TAP fallbacks. The 85-source 4HWC Table-1 source
list is embedded directly so arXiv rate limiting cannot stop the analysis.
An internet connection is required only during this catalog preflight.
Healpy is optional; an
internal HEALPix RING fallback is included.
"""
